It may also fail reasonable-basis suitability if the products themselves were appropriate only for a narrow class of investors and Paul failed to adequately understand or evaluate their risks.

### Regulation Best Interest

Reg BI requires a broker-dealer and associated person, when making a recommendation to a retail customer, to act in the customer’s best interest and not place the broker’s financial or other interests ahead of the customer’s interests.

The likely Reg BI problems include:

- Failure to exercise reasonable diligence, care, and skill;
- Recommendation of products inconsistent with the customers’ profile;
- Excessive concentration in illiquid alternatives;
- High commissions and upfront fees;
- Inadequate consideration of lower-risk, lower-cost alternatives;
- Conflict of interest not adequately mitigated by mere disclosure.

